WEBVTT

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.870
Night School

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.880
So, anyway...

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:47.250
You've become the first class of the 
Seijumonji High School night school.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:51.000
I, Chihiro Chimatsuri, 
will be your homeroom teacher.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.840
I'll be teaching you all subjects.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:53.940
No way.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:54.930
Seriously?

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.470
Are you even qualified to do that?

00:01:56.470 --> 00:02:00.090
I'll now take attendance to confirm the 
presence of all our regulars cast members.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.880
Karate Club Captain 
Masumi Katsuno, blood type O.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:04.900
Here.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:08.280
Your subordinates Kanbara, 
Okada, and Horita.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.980
I hope people remember your names. 
Blood types, unknown.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:12.680
Osu!

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:16.200
Don't say "osu" in my presence!

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:18.080
Dance Club Captain Nami Unten, blood type O.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.660
Yes, ma'am.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.960
Cinema Club Captain 
Maki Watabe, blood type AB.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.010
Cut.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:29.390
Cosplay Club Captain 
Kaoru Konno, blood type B.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:30.540
Here.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.960
Chairman of the Discipline Committee 
Jinko Sumida, blood type—

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.780
I'm a type A perfectionist.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.520
Ostriches are an animal found in zoos,

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.000
but compromise is a word 
not found in my dictionary.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.970
Blood Donation Club Captain 
Mitsugu Bambam, blood type chimera.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:47.050
My name isn't Bambam, 
it's Mitsugu Bamba.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.470
We're only nine students 
and one teacher right now,

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.970
but allow me to introduce 
our transfer student.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.350
Come on out.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.280
Mai in a school uniform, huh?

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.210
Her knock-knee legs look absolutely 
lovely in blue-black tights.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.740
Her handwriting is great.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.280
You can read that?

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.920
My name is Mai Vlad Transylvania.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:29.400
Estimated age 400 years old, 
blood type unknown.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.820
She smuggled herself here from the distant 
Eastern European land of Romania.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:38.920
Make sure you don't rat her out to 
the police or immigration control.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:39.970
Roger!

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:45.530
Now that we've introduced our transfer 
student, let's jump right into it.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:48.690
The most standard of all 
standard school events.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:04:11.980
<b>Stake Festival 2020
Night Class 2B Program</b>

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.230
I knew it.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.390
I thought it was about time this showed up.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:04:00.040
I wish we could take our time democratically 
determining what we'll do,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.870
but since our budget and time are limited,

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.440
based on my arbitrary decision-making 
and personal prejudices,

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.690
the Blood Donation Club's 
program will feature—

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:08.470
A maid café!

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:09.590
An idol café!

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:10.420
A beef bowl shop!

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:11.830
A standing soba shop!

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.520
Fools! That's not what we're doing!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.160
The night school shall participate in the 
school festival by putting on a play.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.980
A play, huh? That's an appropriate choice.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.790
What will we be performing?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:47.050
<b>"Konjiki Yasha"
(The Golden Demon)</b>

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:47.050
<b>"My Second
Brother"</b>

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:47.050
<b>"Lust for Life"</b>

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.160
<i>Kiniro Yorumata</i>?

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.910
Idiot, it's pronounced "Yasha."

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.870
<i>Yasha Yorumata</i>?

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:39.440
Horror.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.010
<i>My Second Brother</i>? What's he second in?

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.990
<i>Lust for Life</i>? Is that a porno?

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:43.920
I'm telling you, let's do horror.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.210
Sounds kind of plain.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.060
Shouldn't we go with something 
flashier for a school festival?

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:50.750
Let's adapt the masterwork 
<i>Castle of Vania</i>.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.460
Good idea. I agree.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:56.070
Don't you think that's a little too cliché?

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:59.230
Won't Ko**mi have something 
to say about that?

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.530
That's why it's Castle of Vania.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.110
Castle of Vania

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.110
Castle of Vania

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.060
I, Kaoru, shall take 
responsibility for the show.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.640
It'll surely be a success.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.780
Well, we do have the perfect leading lady.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:14.120
I knew it.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:21.880
<b>Castle of Vania</b>

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:19.430
The following are the cast and 
staff roles for the play.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:22.550
Mai will play Dracula, lady of the castle.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.780
I look forward to working with everyone.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:32.810
Vampire hunter Simon Belmond will 
be played by Bambam Mitsugu.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.590
Huh?

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:35.410
What? You're unhappy with your role?

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:37.290
No, not really.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:41.020
<i>Well, I guess that means Mai 
and I are the main characters.</i>

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:44.170
Block 1 boss Franken will 
be played by Katsuno.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.880
It's the only thing to do.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.540
Block 2 boss Medusa will be played by Nami.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.980
Aye, sir.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:55.870
Block 3 boss Mummy will for some reason 
by played by me, Chihiro Chimatsuri.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:59.070
And block 4 boss Reaper 
will be played by Kaoru.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.590
I'll handle costumes and play a role.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.070
The *****back, later renamed to 
Flea Man, will be played by Kanbara.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:05.800
Osu!

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:09.730
The making-of photography and direction 
will be handled by Maki Watabe.

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:12.900
All right. I get to film 
a documentary for free.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.690
And production will be handled by—

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.860
You haven't forgotten me, have you?

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:19.660
Just so you know, I don't want to do this.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:23.860
The rest of you will play minor roles 
like crows and skeletons as appropriate.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.310
Rehearsal begins tomorrow.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:27.950
That's all.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:33.080
<b>First Day of Rehearsal</b>

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:43.470
You know, they don't scream in the game.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:46.510
We're following the disk system 
version, so it's fine.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.930
They don't scream in the 
disk system version, either.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.680
Well, whatever.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.890
What kind of rehearsal is this?

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:01.140
I knew I couldn't let you guys handle it.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.480
Do you really think you can 
adapt that masterwork

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.240
for the stage with this lukewarm rehearsal?

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:09.760
Masterwork? Jinko, you used to be a gamer?

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:13.300
Not used to be. I'm still a hardcore gamer.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:18.200
I won't allow you to tarnish that 
masterwork with your inferior remake.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:23.520
Anyway, I know it's sudden, 
but for various reasons,

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.910
allow me to introduce you 
to your new director.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.910
Nobody told us about that.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.300
Doctor, what do you mean by various reasons?

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.560
It's nothing you kids need to know about.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:38.030
Your new director is the Chairman of 
the Discipline Committee Jinko Sumida

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:41.310
whom you all hate so much, 
also known as Jinko Ninagawa.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.580
Her type A blood means she's 
a methodical perfectionist.

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:47.830
I knew I'd be the perfect director.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:48.830
What does that mean?

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:57.590
Now that I'm the director, the lukewarm 
developments we've seen so far...

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.620
...are over!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:01.610
You sound nothing like him.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.160
Ninagawa?

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:06.570
That's Ninagawa...

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:18.350
<b>Stage Name Succession
Ninagawa Jinko</b>

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:22.850
Good, good. Things are 
starting to get exciting.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:27.820
<b>Second Day of Rehearsal</b>

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:27.810
You idiot!

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:36.950
<b>Sirloin</b>

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:32.420
I told you to walk sluggishly!

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:36.940
In what universe is Franken 
agile, you idiot?

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.610
Don't tip-toe!

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:44.020
No walking on the balls of 
your feet either, karate boy!

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:46.990
Forget about karate!

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:51.740
<i>W-Wow, her personality has changed completely.</i>

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.250
What about my personality?

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.920
Whoopsy daisy, my thoughts 
were leaking again.

00:08:55.920 --> 00:09:00.020
Nobody says whoopsy daisy 
anymore, you Sakurajima radish!

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:04.050
Don't you dare sleep!

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:07.300
Medusa, stop playing with the props!

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.040
Reaper, stop dancing around!

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:15.270
Mummy, who gave you permission to smoke?

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:20.280
Why are you filming me?

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:24.270
This degree of perfectionism is annoying.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.800
She's scary.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.900
Your character doesn't go on until the end,

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:32.180
and we probably won't make 
it that far tonight.

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:34.600
You must be hungry, so you can leave.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.490
Don't mind if I do.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.790
Why are you letting her leave?

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:42.020
Understanding the flow of the play is 
the most fundamental part of rehearsal.

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:43.880
You think you can run off early 
just because you're not onstage?

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:44.930
And you call yourself a professional!

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.680
But we're not professionals.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:48.930
I-I'm scared.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:52.090
Mai is anemic. Cut her some slack tonight.

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:53.690
We'll walk her home!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.400
Go to hell!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.240
Mai-tan, are you leav—

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:02.830
I thought I told you to move sluggishly!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:08.250
You lousy actors!

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.440
You must be tired, Mai. I'm sorry.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:32.100
We're doing all of this to procure 
food for you, so try to—

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.450
Is something wrong, Mai?

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:37.730
Did you not like that blood?

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:39.780
It's not that.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:43.510
All I do is cause trouble for everyone.

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:45.660
I really am a worthless vampire.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:48.940
Mai, you don't have to worry about that.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:52.020
Everyone feels the same 
way, but especially me.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:59.890
I've decided to protect you, 
no matter what happens.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:05.090
Why are you willing to do so much for me?

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:10.070
Because since the moment we met, I...

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:16.930
I... I've always...

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:23.160
What are you stammering on 
about, you radish leaf?

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:26.300
Starting tonight, I'll be 
training you with this whip!

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:31.620
Take this, cat!

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.540
Take this, art objects!

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.850
Take this, everything else! 
I'll whip it all!

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:44.760
Stake Festival 2020

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:43.800
<i>Before we knew it, 
the day of the play arrived.</i>

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.580
Wow, look.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:47.360
The entire study body must be here.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:51.350
Night Class Special Production
Castle of Vania

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:49.590
After all, that transfer student 
is the star of the show.

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:51.610
I will I could take night classes, too.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:53.120
Will she really take her clothes off?

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.740
We can't miss this.

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:57.450
Do the teachers really get priority 
admission? Unforgivable.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:58.790
We should denounce them.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:00.100
Hurry up and start the show.

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.590
How long are you going to make us wait?

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.440
Shut up! The fire station will find us!

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:04.920
The cops will show up before that.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:06.070
I told you guys to be quiet!

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:09.080
<i>I wasn't expecting so 
many people to show up.</i>

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.590
<i>I mustn't fail.</i>

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:15.920
<i>If the audience ends up booing, it'll leave 
a permanent stain on the night school—</i>

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:21.250
<i>no, on my directing career.</i>

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.160
Listen up, everyone.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:25.390
The bar-bell will ring soon.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.880
This is the moment of truth that will 
test the worth of the night school.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:35.140
Remember why we shed all that blood, 
sweat, and tears over the past few days.

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:37.250
<i>That's because you threatened us.</i>

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:39.960
Believe in yourselves.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.870
I have zero confidence in us.

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:43.080
Make your hearts one.

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:44.150
<i>We couldn't be less unified.</i>

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:46.280
Let's make this play a success!

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.800
Yeah!

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:49.570
<i>What are you guys cheering for?</i>

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.650
Huh? Where's Mai?

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.130
Mai? Mai!

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.460
She's dead.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.860
What?!

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:04.150
She's obviously not dead.

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:08.370
Anxiety has made her anemic.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:11.520
If we don't give her a transfusion immediately, 
she'll have to drop out of the play.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:12.720
A transfusion?

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:14.720
I'll head home immediately 
to get some blood for her.

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:17.450
Fool. We don't have time for that.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:19.300
The curtains will rise soon.

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:21.340
Why does it have to be now?

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:23.820
This is why amateurs are useless.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.960
Jinko, you've gone too far.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.740
Besides, you're an amateur yourself.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:31.360
Judging by your condition, you've 
got plenty of blood to spare.

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:32.040
What?

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:34.610
<i>The decision Doctor Chihiro 
made in this moment</i>

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:38.360
<i>would determine how the situation 
changed going forward,</i>

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:40.610
<i>but faced with the possibility 
that our leading lady</i>

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.580
<i>might have to drop out 
just before curtains rose,</i>

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:45.510
<i>we couldn't afford to predict that.</i>

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:48.280
Stage right camera 2, are you ready?

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:49.360
Camera 2 ready.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:51.890
Make sure you capture Simon's entrance.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:52.820
Got it.

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:54.260
Balcony camera 3.

00:13:54.260 --> 00:13:55.510
Camera 3 rolling.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.370
Camera 1, start.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:58.450
Camera rolling.

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:01.150
Now give me some great shots.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.230
<i>Not that I'm expecting much.</i>

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:11.950
<b>Self-censored</b>

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:15.870
<b>Act 1 The Dark Road</b>

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:26.090
Ah, I've finally arrived at this castle.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.890
I've been waiting for you, Blood Donation 
Club Captain Mitsugu Bambam.

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:31.830
My name isn't Bambam, it's Mitsugu Bamba.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.170
Okay, okay.

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:39.010
Are you Simon Belmond?

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:44.850
You shall not pass!

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:52.070
Why did dodge that?

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.640
It looked like it would hurt.

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:57.350
Then how about this?

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:04.320
Who are you, Sarah Bryant?

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:06.450
I'm Jill Valentine.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:10.410
<i>What are those idiots doing?!</i>

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.500
The hearts. Release the hearts.

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:13.190
Usu.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:21.380
I won. Now the pocket 
watch sub-weapon is mine.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:22.890
Get 'em!

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:25.640
Get more hearts and your 
pocket watch is unstoppable!

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:27.350
Get more lives!

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:30.330
I don't think so!

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:33.130
Let go! Let go of me, you bitch!

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:34.560
Bitch, bitch, bitch!

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.390
Oh, that's good.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:43.790
Out of the way!

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.920
Out of the way!

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.810
Damn it. My body will never last like this.

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:01.840
Simon, well done making it this far.

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:04.310
But you won't make it past here.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:07.170
Give me a minute. I'm out of breath.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:09.860
The disk system version can't be paused.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.780
Hey, this is real!

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:18.340
Die, die, die, die, die!

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:20.260
Ow!

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:21.850
She stabbed me!

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:27.150
Good, good. Camera 2, move up.

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:29.010
Camera 3, zoom and follow them.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:31.630
Reaper, get out of the way.

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:34.260
What? You don't appear until the next stage.

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:36.440
We don't have time for your lukewarm shit.

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:38.900
A man settles his scores with his fists.

00:16:38.900 --> 00:16:40.260
But I'm a girl.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.000
I was up all night training with Jinko.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.280
Take this!

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.880
Ow, ow, ow!

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:54.250
Move, move, move!

00:16:56.780 --> 00:17:00.530
I'll get you, Simon!

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:05.750
There's nowhere to run, Simon.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:08.920
Your underhanded bastards.

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.270
Die!

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:14.020
I can't breathe. Katsuno, don't 
you think you're overdoing it?

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:18.480
Shut up. I sensed a personal 
grudge behind that whipping!

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:21.310
<b>Personal Grudge
</b>Private malice or spite

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:25.710
How dare you use that move on a girl?!

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:28.600
Nami!

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:33.640
I, Nami Unten, won't allow 
such unrestricted violence.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:38.320
In anime, we enjoy extraterritorial rights.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:41.310
Boys, are you ready?

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:47.340
It's the intermission.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:53.670
That was close, but your 
special item saved you.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:58.400
After that performance, the final 
scene has to go perfectly.

00:17:58.400 --> 00:18:00.840
Dracula Mai, are you ready?

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:03.750
Yes.

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:10.520
I shall put on a perfect 
performance, Jinko-san.

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:17.070
<b>Act 2 The Crimson Showdown</b>

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:24.530
This is what we've been waiting for!

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:25.840
Miss Dracula!

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:27.320
The star of the show!

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:34.210
I am the late Count Dracula's 
lawful wife, Dracula Mai.

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:39.880
There you are, Dracula Mai.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:43.270
The time has finally come to defeat you.

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:45.450
Don't expect that to work out for you.

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:47.420
"Don't expect that to work out for you?"

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:48.820
Was that one of her lines?

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:54.240
Huh? What's gotten into Mai?

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.020
Could it be?

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:59.710
If I'm going to play a vampire, 
I'll play the perfect vampire.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:05.260
<i>Perfect? She's under the 
effects of Jinko's blood!</i>

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:07.950
Simon Belmond, I'm coming for you!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:11.060
Swap with me.

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:16.980
It's okay, Mai.

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:17.660
What?

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:23.260
We were always destined to end up like this.

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:29.640
Now drink to your heart's content.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:44.790
Why are you ignoring the script? 
What are you doing?

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:47.190
Huh?

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:50.290
This isn't good.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.250
The curtains! Lower the curtains!

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:56.350
Stop, stop, stop!

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:58.750
Wow.

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.620
That was intense.

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:04.630
Stop! That hurts!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.900
Mai, calm down! Stop it!

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.970
No!

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.360
There we go.

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:20.660
I suppose I'm partially responsible 
since I fed her Jinko's type A blood.

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:25.980
I can't believe the play went that terribly.

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:38.250
How will I ever apologize to Antonin Artaud, 
Bertolt Brecht—no, to Ninagawa-sensei?

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:39.530
It wasn't that bad.

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:42.430
Listen to those voices.

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:43.440
What?

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:51.510
Let's not disappoint audience 
that watched us until the end.

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:53.580
Line up.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:08.780
Simon Mitsugu and leading lady Dracula Mai.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:10.770
Mai-chan, you're the best!

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:14.290
Even if Mai ends up sucking my 
blood one day, I won't regret it.

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:18.750
Medusa Nami played by Nami Unten.

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:23.240
Reaper Kaoru played by Kaoru Konno.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:24.700
You're just your usual self.

00:21:24.870 --> 00:21:28.150
Franken Katsuno and all the rest.

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:31.170
Osu! Osu, osu, osu, osu!

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:36.850
The there's me, Mummy Chihiro, 
whose role was cut for time,

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:41.820
and director Jinko Sumida.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:44.650
Jinko!

00:21:44.650 --> 00:22:14.970
Jinko! Jinko! Jinko!

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:48.470
That was great and totally random!

00:21:56.680 --> 00:22:01.160
Now you're one of us, Jinko.

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:05.590
You no longer need your discipline or morals.

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:14.980
<b>Castle of Vania
The End</b>

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:59.910
<b>Episode 7 "Day for Night"</b>

00:23:45.830 --> 00:23:47.390
Cut!

00:23:47.390 --> 00:23:49.560
Okay, camera rehearsal looks good.

00:23:49.560 --> 00:23:53.410
You two, I told you boys to 
stop looking at the camera.

00:23:51.050 --> 00:23:54.710
It was supposed to be just 
a little independent film.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.840
This will be a take.
